                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for the feedback. Please check my answers."
                },
                {
                    "file": "ikvm_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Min Wang",
                        "email": "wangmin@phytium.com.cn",
                        "username": "wangmin239"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Jae Hyun Yoo, I believe this line of code is redundant. The variable videoDone is always true before the waitServer function runs. Additionally, as it is shared with the server thread, any updates to its value will be visible to the server thread."
                },
                {
                    "file": "ikvm_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "The 'videoDone = false' inside waitServer(true) is not redundant \u2014 it is the critical piece of synchronization that prevents a race during resize.\n\nHere is the timing that makes it necessary:\n\n  1. setVideoDone()     - videoDone = true, server thread wakes from waitVideo()\n  2. waitServer(true)   - waiting for serverDone == true\n  3.   [server thread]  - exits waitVideo(), runs rfbProcessEvents, sets serverDone = true, loops back\n  4.   [under lock]     - waitServer sees serverDone == true, resets serverDone = false, videoDone = false  \u2190 must happen here\n  5.   [server thread]  - calls waitVideo() again, sees videoDone == false, blocks\n  6. video.resize()     - safe, server is blocked\n  7. server.resize()\n  8. setVideoDone()     - videoDone = true, server unblocks\n\nIf videoDone is not reset to false inside the lock at step 4, there is a window between steps 3 and 5 where the server thread calls waitVideo(), sees videoDone still true, and passes straight through \u2014 racing with video.resize() and server.resize().\n\nThe concern is not about visibility \u2014 it is about ordering. Resetting videoDone under the same lock that waitVideo() also acquires creates a happens-before guarantee: by the time the server thread next observes videoDone, it will always see false. Without the reset inside the lock, that guarantee does not exist.\n\nIn fact, this is exactly the bug that existed in the original code: videoDone = false was set outside the lock, leaving a race window. Moving it inside waitServer() under the lock is the fix,not dead code.\n\nPlease see below journal logs.\n\nThis is log pattern from original code:\n```\nMay 25 23:21:22 qcom-bmc-ast2600-d6bc0bf5efe0 obmc-ikvm[315]: Failed to query timings Link has been severed\nMay 25 23:21:23 qcom-bmc-ast2600-d6bc0bf5efe0 obmc-ikvm[315]: 25/05/2026 23:21:23 Pixel format for client 127.0.0.1:\nMay 25 23:21:23 qcom-bmc-ast2600-d6bc0bf5efe0 obmc-ikvm[315]: 25/05/2026 23:21:23   32 bpp, depth 24, little endian\nMay 25 23:21:23 qcom-bmc-ast2600-d6bc0bf5efe0 obmc-ikvm[315]: 25/05/2026 23:21:23   true colour: max r 255 g 255 b 255, shift r 0 g 8 b 16\n```\n\nAnd, this is log pattern after applying this fix:\n```\nMay 25 23:43:42 qcom-bmc-ast2600-d6bc0bf5efe0 obmc-ikvm[308]: Failed to query timings\nMay 25 23:43:42 qcom-bmc-ast2600-d6bc0bf5efe0 obmc-ikvm[308]: 25/05/2026 23:43:42 Sending rfbEncodingExtDesktopSize for size (1152x864)\n```\n\nThe \"Link has been severed\" message from the original code is the kernel's string representation of ENOLINK, returned by the V4L2 driver when a timings query (e.g. VIDIOC_QUERYSTD) fails because the video signal between the host GPU and the kernel video capture engine is momentarily lost. This is expected behavior during a resolution switch \u2014 the host briefly drops sync while renegotiating timings for the new mode.\n\nBefore the patch, the process stalled at this point due to the deadlock, so the resize can't be completed properly. After the patch, \"Link has been severed\" no longer appears because the resize path now proceeds correctly past the transient signal loss and delivers rfbEncodingExtDesktopSize to the client with the new resolution, confirming the fix works as intended."
                },
                {
                    "file": "ikvm_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Min Wang",
                        "email": "wangmin@phytium.com.cn",
                        "username": "wangmin239"
                    },
                    "message": "Maybe I wasn't clear. Line 34 is unnecessary. Please remove it and attempt to reproduce the deadlock."
                },
                {
                    "file": "ikvm_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Min Wang",
                        "email": "wangmin@phytium.com.cn",
                        "username": "wangmin239"
                    },
                    "message": "Based on the logs you shared, the deadlock tends to occur on the dual-core AST2600, while it does not manifest on the single-core AST2500. I have previously resolved a similar deadlock issue on single-core SoCs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "ikvm_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "I checked the flow again, and you\u2019re right \u2014 the setVideoDone() call on line 34 is not needed, so I removed it. And, I know the change history and saw that you fixed the deadlock issue on via the https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/obmc-ikvm/+/71609 . Nice fix."
                }
            ],
